 "description": "Create a new brand for a product that is waiting on\n`brand_decision_required`, and attach the product to it.\n\nUse this when the product belongs to a company the account has no brand\nfor yet \u2014 the usual case when someone brings a new store. For a product\nimported from a URL the brand's name, voice, target market and keywords\nare taken from what the storefront scrape drafted; the user can rename\nit with `name`. For a product created from photos nothing was detected\n(`detected_brand_name` is null), so `name` is required and `voice`,\n`target_market` and `keywords` should come from the user \u2014 ask them how\nthe brand sounds and who it sells to. Anything you pass overrides the\ndetected value.\n\nAsk the user before calling this. It consumes one of the plan's brand\nslots, and on a plan that has run out this fails with a brand-limit\nerror \u2014 at which point the choices are to attach the product to an\nexisting brand with `set_product_brand`, to re-point an existing brand\nat this identity with `set_product_brand` and `replace_identity: true`,\nor to upgrade.\n\nOnce this returns, the video direction starts drafting: poll\n`get_product` until `video_direction.drafting` is false.\n\nDirection drafting sends product facts, photos and brand context to\nan external AI service when the product is ready and its brand is settled.\n\nThis does not spend credits.\n",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "keywords": {
    "description": "Optional. A few short keywords for the brand's themes and audience \u2014 generic enough to survive a different product.",
    "items": {
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "name": {
    "description": "The brand's name. Optional when a storefront name was detected (it overrides it); required for a product created from photos.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "product_id": {
    "description": "The product waiting on a brand decision.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "target_market": {
    "description": "Optional. Who the brand sells to, as \"Region, Language\" (e.g. \"US, English\"). Sets the market and spoken language of every video on the brand.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "voice": {
    "description": "Optional. How the brand talks, in a sentence or two \u2014 the tone every video direction is drafted in.",
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "product_id"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
